+## 6. What remains unexamined
+
+1. The exact record of the Ministry→Judiciary request and declination was not located in `records/`; the claim is reported baseline, not verified here.
+2. No consumer inventory: do any scripts read *all* `suite-compliance-*.json` files, or require each `details_ref` to resolve to a distinct file? (Grep of government scripts for the glob was not completed.) This determines whether pointer remapping (§3.3) is sufficient.
+3. Actual filesystem free space, inode count, and the `economy-resources.py` time-to-exhaustion forecast were not inspected; urgency (H6) is unquantified.
+4. Integrity of the 529 canonical copies was not independently verified beyond the writer's own `details_sha256`; a full hash manifest and sample audit are untested.
+5. Concurrency: behaviour of a dedup/quarantine pass racing the ~4-minute live writer (including `.tmp` files and `replace()` atomicity) was not tested.
+6. Grace-period restoration (reversing a `quarantined.tsv` row) and the independent before/after measurement were not exercised — no dry-run was performed against live state.
+7. Whether the `per_change` entries' ~98.7% `unreadable` status reflects a measurement defect (and thus whether these snapshots have evidentiary value worth bounding at all) is a separate Judiciary question, out of scope here.
+8. Legal nuance: whether *deduplication* (not just deletion) of evidence is restricted under Act 15 was not resolved; the prior declination concerned rotation, not dedup specifically.
